Chapter: DeskPillDoubleClickTest
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A second click on the same pill inside 400 ms puts the window back away. The
 decision is a comparison over an id and an interval, so it is decidable here
 with no band, no pointer and no clock.

 IT CALLS `dk-dclick`, WHICH IS THE FUNCTION `desk-dispatch` ITSELF BRANCHES
 ON, and the two cell writers beside it. A test that re-derived "same id and
 close enough in time" would be a shadow of the dispatch's own test.

 TIME IS A TICK AND A RATE, and every row uses a rate of 1000 so a tick reads
 as a millisecond.

Section: Body

  pc-yn : Boolean -> Text
  pc-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  pc-tps : Integer = 1000

 THE ID IS WHAT MAKES IT A DOUBLE-CLICK RATHER THAN TWO CLICKS. `different
 pill` is the row that matters: it is inside the interval and must still
 answer no, and without it a rule that only looked at the clock would pass
 every other row here.

  pc-case : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean -> Text
  pc-case (label) (last) (fid) (el) (tps) (want) =
    label & ": last " & integer-to-text last & " now " & integer-to-text fid
    & " after " & integer-to-text el & " ms at rate " & integer-to-text tps
    & " -> " & pc-yn (dk-dclick last fid el tps)
    & "  wanted " & pc-yn want
    & "  " & pc-yn (dk-dclick last fid el tps == want)

 THE RECORD ROUND-TRIPS AND THE CLEAR UNDOES IT, asked through the cells
 rather than by trusting the writers. The pair is read back and then put to
 `dk-dclick` itself, so the row measures what the dispatch would decide on the
 next click rather than what the cells happen to hold.

  pc-note : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  pc-note (ds) (fid) (now) =
    let n = dk-pillc-note ds fid now
    in "noted " & integer-to-text fid & " at " & integer-to-text now
       & " -> cell " & integer-to-text (peek-32 ds dk-pillc-cell)
       & " t " & integer-to-text (peek-32 ds dk-pillc-t-cell)
       & "  a second click 100 ms later doubles "
       & pc-yn (dk-dclick (peek-32 ds dk-pillc-cell) fid 100 pc-tps)

  pc-clear : Integer, Integer -> Text
  pc-clear (ds) (fid) =
    let c = dk-pillc-clear ds
    in "cleared -> cell " & integer-to-text (peek-32 ds dk-pillc-cell)
       & "  none " & integer-to-text desk-focus-none
       & "  the same click 100 ms later doubles "
       & pc-yn (dk-dclick (peek-32 ds dk-pillc-cell) fid 100 pc-tps)
       & "  (it must not, which is what stops a third click firing again)"

Section: Opening

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in act
      print-line-uni ("double-click window " & integer-to-text dk-dclick-ms & " ms")
      print-line-uni (pc-case "the pair      " desk-focus-calc desk-focus-calc 120 pc-tps True)
      print-line-uni (pc-case "too slow      " desk-focus-calc desk-focus-calc 900 pc-tps False)
      print-line-uni (pc-case "different pill" desk-focus-calc desk-focus-clkp 120 pc-tps False)
      print-line-uni (pc-case "nothing before" desk-focus-none desk-focus-calc 120 pc-tps False)
      print-line-uni (pc-case "exactly 400   " desk-focus-calc desk-focus-calc 400 pc-tps True)
      print-line-uni (pc-case "just past 400 " desk-focus-calc desk-focus-calc 401 pc-tps False)
      print-line-uni (pc-case "no hpet       " desk-focus-calc desk-focus-calc 120 0 False)
      print-line-uni (pc-note ds desk-focus-calc 7000)
      print-line-uni (pc-clear ds desk-focus-calc)
    end

